  "response": "## Solution\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem with:\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(–|¬D) = 0.95, so P(+|¬D) = 0.05\n\n**P(+)** = P(D)·P(+|D) + P(¬D)·P(+|¬D)\n= (0.002)(0.98) + (0.998)(0.05)\n= 0.00196 + 0.0499\n= 0.05186\n\n**P(D|+)** = [P(D)·P(+|D)] / P(+)\n= 0.00196 / 0.05186\n≈ 0.037794\n\nSo the probability the person actually has the condition, given a positive test, is about **3.78%**.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
